## Claim
Text: "People who do not vote for the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) in the 2020 elections will not get the COVID vaccine free of cost."
Claim author: Firoz Khan 
Claim date: October 22, 2020
Claim origin: https://twitter.com/sirfirozkhan/status/1319360671729922048

## Initial Q&A
### Did the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) release an election manifesto for the 2020 Bihar Legislative Assembly election promising free COVID-19 vaccines to the public?
Answer: Yes, the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) released an election manifesto for the 2020 Bihar Assembly polls promising the "free distribution of vaccine against COVID-19 once it is approved by the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR)." During the launch of the manifesto, Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman confirmed this, stating, "As soon as COVID-19 vaccine is available for production on a mass scale, every person in Bihar will get free vaccination."

Source URL: https://www.thehindu.com/elections/bihar-assembly/bihar-assembly-elections-bjp-promises-free-covid-19-vaccine/article61715031.ece

### What were the exact words used by the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) in its October 2020 election campaign regarding the distribution of free COVID-19 vaccines?
Answer: During the October 2020 election campaign in Bihar, Union Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman announced the BJP's promise, stating, "As soon as COVID-19 vaccine is available for production on a mass scale, every person in Bihar will get free vaccination. This is the first promise mentioned in our poll manifesto." Additionally, the party's manifesto officially promised the "free distribution of vaccine against COVID-19 once it is approved by the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR)."

Source URL: https://www.thehindu.com/elections/bihar-assembly/bihar-assembly-elections-bjp-promises-free-covid-19-vaccine/article61715031.ece

### Did any official spokesperson or leader of the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) state that free COVID-19 vaccines would only be given to people who voted for the BJP in the 2020 elections?
Answer: Based on the provided search result, no BJP leader or spokesperson stated that free vaccines would only be given to those who voted for the party. Instead, Union Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman released the BJP election manifesto promising that once a vaccine is cleared for large-scale production, "we will make it available to the people of Bihar free of cost."

Source URL: https://www.newsclick.in/Bihar-Elections-BJP-Promises-Free-COVID-19-Vaccines-Opposition-%23-VaccinePolitics

### Is there any official policy or directive from the Government of India that links the distribution of COVID-19 vaccines to an individual's voting record or political affiliation?
Answer: No, there is no official policy linking COVID-19 vaccine distribution to political affiliation or voting records. According to the search result, government officials stated that the vaccine will be distributed under a special immunization programme based on priority groups—such as healthcare professionals, frontline workers, and high-risk age groups—with the Centre procuring it directly to make it available free of cost. Furthermore, Union Health Minister Harsh Vardhan assured that the government is working to "ensure that there is a fair and equitable distribution of vaccines" and to "ensure that the vaccine reaches the last person."

Source URL: https://m.economictimes.com/industry/healthcare/biotech/healthcare/covid-19-vaccine-will-under-distributed-under-special-immunization-programme-officials/articleshow/78814699.cms

### How does the Government of India plan to verify who receives the COVID-19 vaccine, and does this verification process involve checking political party support or voting history?
Answer: The Government of India plans to identify and verify vaccine recipients based on priority groups—such as healthcare professionals, frontline workers, and individuals over 50 or with co-morbidities—using "an integrated IT platform e-Vin (electronic Vaccine Intelligent Network)" and an enhanced digital platform from the Universal Immunisation Programme. The search result does not contain any information suggesting that this verification process involves checking political party support or voting history.

Source URL: https://m.economictimes.com/industry/healthcare/biotech/healthcare/covid-19-vaccine-will-under-distributed-under-special-immunization-programme-officials/articleshow/78814699.cms

### Did the Government of India announce a nationwide policy to provide COVID-19 vaccines free of cost to all Indian citizens regardless of state elections?
Answer: Based on the provided search result, the Government of India did not announce a nationwide policy to provide COVID-19 vaccines free of cost to all citizens. Instead, BJP IT cell head Amit Malviya clarified that the "centre will provide vaccine to states at a nominal price," leaving it up to the individual state governments "to decide if they want to give it free or otherwise."

