## Final Judgement
### Step-by-Step Thoughts

1. **Summarize key insights**: The retrieved evidence shows that the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) promised free COVID-19 vaccines to "every person in Bihar" in its 2020 election manifesto, with no conditions regarding how individuals voted. Furthermore, official plans from the Government of India indicate that vaccine distribution is organized under a special immunization programme based on priority groups (such as healthcare and frontline workers) and managed via the e-Vin digital platform. There is no policy, directive, or mechanism linking vaccine eligibility to political affiliation or voting history, nor did any BJP official state that free vaccines would be restricted to BJP voters. Because the evidence is clear and comprehensive, no further investigation is required.
2. **Determine the decision**: The claim states that people who do not vote for the BJP will not get the vaccine free of cost. However, the evidence shows that the BJP's promise was for all residents of Bihar, and the actual government distribution criteria are based strictly on public health priority groups, completely independent of voting records. Therefore, the claim is explicitly contradicted by the facts.
3. **Formulate the conclusion**: I will state the decision as `refuted` and briefly explain why based on the summarized evidence.

### Conclusion

Based on the recorded evidence, the claim that individuals who do not vote for the BJP will be denied free COVID-19 vaccines is completely false. The BJP's 2020 election manifesto promised free vaccines to all residents of Bihar, and the Government of India's official vaccine distribution guidelines rely strictly on medical priority groups and digital verification systems that do not track political affiliation or voting history. Therefore, the decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted as there is no official policy or statement linking COVID-19 vaccine distribution to political affiliation or voting records. In its 2020 Bihar election manifesto, the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) promised free vaccines to every person in Bihar once approved, without any voting conditions, as reported by [The Hindu](https://www.thehindu.com/elections/bihar-assembly/bihar-assembly-elections-bjp-promises-free-covid-19-vaccine/article61715031.ece) and [Newsclick](https://www.newsclick.in/Bihar-Elections-BJP-Promises-Free-COVID-19-Vaccines-Opposition-%23-VaccinePolitics). Furthermore, official plans from the Government of India, detailed by [The Economic Times](https://m.economictimes.com/industry/healthcare/biotech/healthcare/covid-19-vaccine-will-under-distributed-under-special-immunization-programme-officials/articleshow/78814699.cms), show that vaccines are distributed under a special immunization programme based strictly on medical priority groups and verified through the e-Vin digital platform, completely independent of political support. Additionally, [India TV News](https://www.indiatvnews.com/opinion/news-bihar-election-2020-poll-promises-jobs-development-standards-of-living-bjp-rjd-jdu-ljp-pm-modi-659069) noted that individual state governments decide whether to provide the vaccine for free after procuring it from the Centre.